SUMMARY
SALAMA Website was created to help tackle the emerging Gender Based Violence 
by creating one conscise webpage where : you can report a case ,seek aid from professionals 
,volunteer and create awareness on the GBV .The webpage also contains Emergence contacts to 
be able to get help as soon as possible.The webpage also accepts donation via Mpesa, credit card bank transfer
Lastly,The webpage also allows the user to filter by counties and type of help and it also features a dark mode

Things the app may store
• Users/Accounts — survivors, NGO staff/case workers, admins, service providers 
• Incident Reports — the core GBV report (type, date, location, description, evidence attachments) 
• Cases — a case worker's tracked file, possibly linked to one or more reports 
• Support Services — shelters, counselors, legal aid providers, hospitals/clinics 
• Service Providers — organizations/individuals offering the above services 
•	Donate-Record of the transactions
•	

Actions a user may take
• Reports: create, view (own only), edit, delete, submit anonymously, attach evidence, mark status (open/in review/closed), escalate 
• Cases: create, view, assign to case worker, update status, add notes, close/reopen, transfer to another worker 
• Services: search, filter (by type/location/availability), view details, bookmark/save 
• Messages: send, read, mark as read, delete, block/report a contact 
• Documents: upload, view, download, delete, restrict access 
• Users/Accounts: register, log in, log out, edit profile, verify identity (for staff), deactivate/delete account, reset password 
•	Donation-The User may make a donation to the web page via Mpesa , credit card or bank transfer

